#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:140
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`fsh-cone --changed` (scripts/fsh-cone.ts) over the changed files: the forward cone is what to rebuild, the backward cone is what to check out."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:289
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A preview never seeds the shared cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:97
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A push to a PR branch (review path) or to main / a release (publish path). Both run this process; only the publish path may seed the cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:32
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "An incremental build for a FHIR Implementation Guide: compile, validate and re-render only the dependency cone of a change, then gate on QA and deploy. One change (a PR push or a push to main) runs: restore the derived state, compute the change's dependency cone, compile and validate only the cone against the warm validator, re-render the cone's records, rebuild the meta-index, assemble the site, gate on QA, then deploy; on main or a release only, seed the cache from the green build. An unusable cache falls back to a full build; an environment error stops the run and logs why. Advisory, like the other content-type pipelines: the package that owns the content owns what adequate means."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:196
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered by Task_Validate — the cone's resources checked against the warm validator. `yes` goes on to re-render the cone's records. `no` logs the findings on the change's bean and returns them to the author. A validator that could not start is could-not-determine and does not take `yes`."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:109
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered by the exit code of `ig-cache restore` (Task_Restore): 0 is a usable cache and takes `yes`, into the cone machinery. 1 (a miss) or 3 (present but unusable) takes `no`, to the full publisher build, whose outputs become the records the next seed writes. Exit 2 (an environment error — the cache could not be read, which says nothing about whether it is usable) takes `environment error`: the run stops and the error is logged, so a broken cache store is not hidden behind a slow full build."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:283
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered by the push that started the process. `PR branch` is the review path: deploy the preview, which never seeds the shared cache. `main / release` is the publish path: deploy the site after a human has authorised the release, then seed the cache (Task_Seed). Only this branch reaches the lane allowed to touch the shared cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:244
#. Diagram label
msgid "Assemble the site"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:245
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Assemble the site from the merged records: the IG template and a Jekyll build over output/. Only site assembly happens here — every artefact record already exists."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:127
#. Diagram label
msgid "Build stopped: environment error"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:108
#. Diagram label
msgid "Cache usable?"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:101
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Calls the harness's one cache process, `Process_Cache` (cat-harness, skill `cache-first-ci`), with this IG build as its consumer. Its plan restores only the caches this target needs: the layers ref first, then this IG's AST and the Publisher's terminology cache (`input-cache/txcache/`) as the declared `fhir-ast` cache (`caches/fhir-ast.cache.json`), whose component process is `ig-ast-cache.bpmn` and whose verify is that process's \"valid for this commit?\". Under it, `ig-cache restore` still answers 0 usable, 1 miss, 2 environment error, 3 present but unusable (corrupt or mismatched, such as a moved toolchain), and the component prints its `cached-step` line (hit, warm or miss)."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:227
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Combine the restored per-artefact records with the cone's freshly rendered ones into one complete set, so the meta-index rebuild that follows has every artefact's record and never re-derives one."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:170
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Compile the restricted checkout with SUSHI — the cone's FSH, not the whole IG. A build optimisation, not a validation shortcut: SUSHI compiling is not conformance, so a green compile goes on to validation rather than standing in for it."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:139
#. Diagram label
msgid "Compute the cone of the change"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:262
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Decided in the reviewer's QC gate (Task_Qa, `quality-control`) over qa.json, the aggregate of per-artefact outcomes, reading the cone's rows first. `no` files each QC finding as a bean, checking for an existing one first, and returns the findings to the author. `yes` goes on to deploy."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:288
