msgid "Restricted checkout of the backward cone"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:150
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Review path: the reviewer sees what this change rebuilds — how many artefacts, and whether a hub (a shared RuleSet, CQL library or value set) is touched — before the build finishes. On main it is a log line."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:252
#. Diagram label
msgid "Run QC gates on the aggregate QA"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:310
#. Diagram label
msgid "Seed the cache from the green build"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:79
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Sees the change's shape before the build finishes — Task_ConeReport names what will rebuild and whether a shared hub is touched, posted while the checkout is still running — then gates on Task_Qa by reading the cone's own rows in the aggregate first. On a PR branch it also deploys the preview itself, but never seeds the shared cache: that stays Lane_PubMgr's, reached only past Gateway_Path on main or a release."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:96
#. Diagram label
msgid "Source changed"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:47
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Starts the run with a source change, and owns every failure branch before the process ends rather than just stopping: Gateway_Valid's `no`, Gateway_QcPass's `no` and Gateway_Restore's `environment error` each write to the work plan here, in Task_LogFindings, Task_QcBeans and Task_LogEnvError, before EndEvent_Findings, EndEvent_FindingsQc or EndEvent_EnvError. A run that stops short always leaves a record of why. The work plan is a data store these tasks write to, not a lane of its own."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:169
#. Diagram label
msgid "SUSHI on the restricted tank"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:178
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The validator's server mode holds the loaded dependency packages, snapshots and expansions in its session cache. Cold start loads the restored derived FHIR rather than regenerating it."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:235
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The whole-IG aggregates only — artifacts, TOC, canonicals, expansions, package, QA aggregate. Never re-derives an artefact: a missing record is a miss (exit 1), not a silent rebuild."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:71
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Two duties. Task_FullBuild is the fallback when Gateway_Restore finds the cache unusable: it bypasses the cone machinery and reaches Task_Qa on its own. Task_ContextLoad and Task_Validate hold the loaded dependency packages and expansions warm across runs, which makes validating a handful of cone files cheap; losing that warm state is a cache miss and routes to the fallback."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:195
#. Diagram label
msgid "Valid?"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:187
#. Diagram label
msgid "Validate the cone (fhir_validate)"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:188
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Validate the cone's resources against the warm validator and report the cone that was checked. A validator that could not start is could-not-determine, never a pass with no findings. A green cone is not a green IG: a profile the change did not touch can still be broken by it."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/collab/processes/content/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:202
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Validation failed: record the findings on the change's bean, so the work plan says what blocks it. Check before creating — beans create is not idempotent."
msgstr ""

